}
\details{
Wraps the ESPN core-v2 team record endpoint
\code{sports.core.api.espn.com/v2/sports/football/leagues/college-football/seasons/{year}/types/{season_type}/teams/{team_id}/record}.
ESPN returns several record items per team (overall, home record, away
record, vs. conference), each carrying ~20 summary stats. This wrapper
flattens that to long format: one row per (record-item x stat). The long
shape absorbs ESPN adding or retiring stat keys across seasons. Pivot
wider with \code{\link[tidyr:pivot_wider]{tidyr::pivot_wider()}} keyed on \code{stat_name} for a wide table.

When \code{team_detail = TRUE} (the default) the ESPN team catalog
(\code{\link[=espn_cfb_teams]{espn_cfb_teams()}}) is fetched once and friendly team fields are joined
in next to the \code{team_id} column -- \code{team_name}, \code{team_abbreviation},
\code{team_location}, \code{team_display_name}, \code{team_short_display_name},
\code{team_nickname}, \code{team_color}, \code{team_alternate_color},
\code{team_logo_href}, and \code{team_logo_dark_href}, inserted immediately after
\code{team_id}.
A catalog failure degrades to \code{NA} rather than erroring the wrapper. Set
\code{team_detail = FALSE} to skip the catalog fetch and the join.
